    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0394" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.62/1258: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The King of Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vittorio Emanuele</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-30">August 30,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am grateful to you for your interest. I have immediately transmitted your
                        message<anchor n="80" xml:id="d382-f1"/> to my Government. As is known to
                    all, there has been done and there is being done by us whatever is possible to
                    bring about a peace with justice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vittorio Emanuele</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="80" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 77, August 23, 11 a.m., to the Ambassador in Italy, <ref
                        target="#pg351">p. 351</ref>.</p>
